<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1862</h1><p class="ref-lede">1862 in world history: 45 events, 20 births, 15 deaths, 1 work, 5 states founded and 2 that came to an end. 1,045 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1858">1858</a><a href="/years/1859">1859</a><a href="/years/1860">1860</a><a href="/years/1861">1861</a><a href="/years/1862" aria-current="page">1862</a><a href="/years/1863">1863</a><a href="/years/1864">1864</a><a href="/years/1865">1865</a><a href="/years/1866">1866</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-19">19 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Union forces win the Battle of Mill Springs in Kentucky</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Union troops defeated Confederate forces near present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nancy">Nancy</a>, Kentucky, ending an early Confederate offensive in south central Kentucky. It was the Confederacy's first significant defeat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-10">10 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Union vessels destroy the Confederate Mosquito Fleet</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After the Battle of Roanoke Island, ships of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states-navy">US Navy</a>'s North Atlantic Blockading Squadron attacked the Confederate Mosquito Fleet on the Pasquotank River near Elizabeth City, North Carolina. The Union took the town and the fleet was destroyed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-9">9 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Monitor and Virginia fight the first battle between ironclads</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At Hampton Roads, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, USS Monitor and the Confederate CSS Virginia fought for hours without decisive damage. The duel showed that wooden warships were obsolete.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-23">23 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Stonewall Jackson opens his Valley campaign at Kernstown</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The First Battle of Kernstown, in Frederick County and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winchester">Winchester</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, opened Stonewall Jackson's campaign through the Shenandoah Valley. Although a Confederate defeat, the engagement distracted Federal efforts to capture Richmond.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-5">5 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">McClellan's Union army begins the siege of Yorktown</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Marching up the Peninsula from Fort Monroe toward Richmond, George B. McClellan's Army of the Potomac met John B. Magruder's small Confederate force behind the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warwick">Warwick</a> Line at Yorktown and settled in for a siege, which lasted until 4 May.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-12">12 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Union raiders seize the locomotive General in the Andrews Raid</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Union volunteers led by the civilian scout James J. Andrews commandeered the locomotive The General at Big Shanty, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, and took it north toward Chattanooga, damaging the Western and Atlantic Railroad. Confederate forces chased them for 87 miles.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zaragoza.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-5">5 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mexican army defeats the French at Puebla</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">General Ignacio <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a>'s outnumbered troops repulsed a French assault on Puebla. The victory, marked as Cinco de Mayo, delayed but did not prevent the French occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-5">5 May</a> · Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-puebla">Battle of Puebla</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Puebla was fought on 5 May 1862 during the French intervention in Mexico, when Mexican troops under General Ignacio Zaragoza repulsed a French assault on the forts above Puebla.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-30">30 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Union forces under Halleck capture Corinth, Mississippi</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The month-long siege of Corinth, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a>, ended when Union forces under Major General Henry W. Halleck took the town from retreating Confederate forces under General P. G. T. Beauregard. Corinth was a critical rail junction.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-31">31 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Johnston and Smith attack McClellan's army outside Richmond</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Confederate forces under Joseph E. Johnston and G.W. Smith attacked George B. McClellan's Union army at Seven Pines, outside the Confederate capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richmond-virginia">Richmond, Virginia</a>. Johnston was wounded, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee">Robert E. Lee</a> soon took command of the army.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee">Robert E. Lee</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mississippi-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-6">6 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Union forces win the First Battle of Memphis on the Mississippi</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The naval battle just north of Memphis, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a>, was a crushing defeat for the Confederates and left the city in Union hands. It was the last time civilians with no prior military experience were permitted to command ships in combat.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi River</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-9">9 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Stonewall Jackson ends his Valley campaign with a win at Port Republic</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Jackson's Army of the Valley won its most costly battle of the Shenandoah Valley campaign at Port Republic, in Rockingham County, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>. With Cross Keys it forced the Union armies to retreat, leaving Jackson free to reinforce <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee">Robert E. Lee</a> near Richmond.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee">Robert E. Lee</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-1">1 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Union guns repel Lee's assaults at Malvern Hill</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Massed Union artillery shattered Confederate attacks at Malvern Hill near Richmond, the last of the Seven Days Battles. Though McClellan withdrew afterwards, Lee's costly assaults ended the campaign.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-12">12 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln signs the act creating the Army Medal of Honor</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">President Lincoln signed a resolution authorising the Medal of Honor for army soldiers who distinguished themselves by gallantry. It remains the highest US military decoration.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-17">17 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Antietam, America's bloodiest single day</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Union and Confederate armies suffered about 23,000 casualties along Antietam <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a>. Lee's retreat gave Lincoln the victory he needed to announce the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emancipation-proclamation">Emancipation Proclamation</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-19">19 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Rosecrans halts Sterling Price's advance at the Battle of Iuka</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At Iuka, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a>, Union Brigadier General William S. Rosecrans stopped the advance of the Confederate Army of the West under Major General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pound-sterling">Sterling</a> Price. It was the opening battle of the Iuka–Corinth Campaign of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/taiping-rebellion" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taiping-rebellion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-21">21 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Ever Victorious Army wins at Cixi but loses its commander</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing dynasty</a>'s European-trained Ever Victorious Army defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiping-rebellion">Taiping</a> forces at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empress-dowager-cixi">Cixi</a>, but its commander, the American <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> Frederick Townsend Ward, was mortally wounded. His death began a period of decline for the force under Henry Andres Burgevine.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiping-rebellion">Taiping</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-22">22 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln issues the preliminary Emancipation Proclamation</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Lincoln announced that enslaved people in states still in rebellion on 1 January 1863 would be declared free. The war for the Union became also a war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-3">3 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Earl Van Dorn attacks Rosecrans at the Second Battle of Corinth</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Confederate forces under Earl Van Dorn attacked the Union defences around Corinth, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a>, in a battle that lasted two days. For the second time in the Iuka–Corinth Campaign, William S. Rosecrans defeated a Confederate army.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-8">8 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Perryville halts the Confederate invasion of Kentucky</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">West of Perryville, Kentucky, Braxton Bragg's Confederate Army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> won a tactical victory over part of Don Carlos Buell's Union Army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio">Ohio</a>, but then withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a>. The Union kept control of Kentucky for the rest of the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-1">1 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln's second State of the Union presses for ending slavery</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In his second State of the Union Address to the 37th Congress, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a> reaffirmed the necessity of ending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emancipation-proclamation">Emancipation Proclamation</a> of a month later made more than 3.5 million people enslaved in the Confederate states legally free.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emancipation-proclamation">Emancipation Proclamation</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/yazoo-river" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yazoo-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-12">12 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">USS Cairo sinks after striking a mine on the Yazoo River</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Union river gunboat USS <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>, lead ship of the City-class casemate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ironclad">ironclads</a>, was sunk by a mine on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazoo-river">Yazoo River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a>, which joins the Mississippi River just north of Vicksburg.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazoo-river">Yazoo River</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-31">31 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Stones River begins near Murfreesboro, Tennessee</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Bragg's Confederate Army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a> and Rosecrans's Union Army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumberland">Cumberland</a> began a three-day battle near Murfreesboro, Tennessee, with the highest casualty rate of the war's major battles. It ended in a costly Union victory that lifted Northern morale.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-saigon-1862" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-saigon-1862.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-saigon-1862">Treaty of Saigon (1862)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Saigon, signed on 5 June 1862, ended the first phase of the French conquest of southern Vietnam.</p></div></li></ol></section>
