<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/nguyen-dynasty"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nguyen%20dynasty.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nguyen dynasty</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Treaty of Saigon cedes three provinces of Cochinchina to France</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-buganda"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Buganda.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Buganda</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">John Hanning Speke reaches the court of Mutesa I</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-tonga"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Tonga.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Tonga</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">George Tupou I’s code frees commoners from forced service to chiefs</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/olmecs"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Olmecs.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Olmecs</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The first known colossal head comes to light at Tres Zapotes, described by José María Melgar y Serrano</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/self-strengthening-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Self-Strengthening%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Self-Strengthening Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Tongwen Guan opens in Beijing to train interpreters, later adding mathematics and astronomy</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Confederate%20States%20of%20America.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Confederate States of America</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Davis is inaugurated under the permanent constitution for a six-year term; the Permanent Congress has opened in Richmond on 18 February.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Confederate%20States%20of%20America.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Confederate States of America</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 16 April the Confederate Congress imposes the first mass conscription on North American territory, making white men from 18 to 35 soldiers for three years.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Confederate%20States%20of%20America.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Confederate States of America</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lee's invasion of Maryland is turned back at Antietam and Bragg's of Kentucky fails; Lincoln's preliminary Emancipation Proclamation ends British and French thoughts of recognition.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/lili-uokalani"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lili%CA%BBuokalani.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Liliʻuokalani</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">She marries the American-born John Owen Dominis on 16 September and moves into Washington Place in Honolulu</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/tlingit"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tlingit.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tlingit</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Pacific Northwest smallpox epidemic kills about 60% of the Mainland Tlingit</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/otto-von-bismarck"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Otto%20von%20Bismarck.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Otto von Bismarck</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Appointed Minister President and Foreign Minister of Prussia in September and gives his 'iron and blood' speech to the Budget Committee</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/giuseppe-garibaldi"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Giuseppe%20Garibaldi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Giuseppe Garibaldi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Marches on Rome under the slogan &quot;Rome or Death&quot; and is wounded and captured by government troops at Aspromonte</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-puebla"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Puebla.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Puebla</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The agreements among the allies at Orizaba break down, and the French defeat a small Mexican force at Escamela and capture Orizaba</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-puebla"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Puebla.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Puebla</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lorencez's columns fail to storm the forts of Guadalupe and Loreto above Puebla</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-puebla"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Puebla.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Puebla</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The French retire to Orizaba to await reinforcements from France</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-puebla"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Puebla.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Puebla</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Juárez declares the anniversary of the battle a national holiday</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/new-orleans"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/New%20Orleans.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>New Orleans</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A Union fleet takes the city after passing Forts Jackson and St. Philip</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/moai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Moai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Moai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Slave traders raided the island, and within a year those who remained were sick or injured and lacking leadership</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/manifest-destiny"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Manifest%20destiny.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Manifest destiny</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Homestead Act offers western land to settlers for almost nothing</span></li></ul></section>
